1. Problem Statement

Write a C program to perform the following operations on an undirected graph using an adjacency matrix:

A. Insertion of a vertex: Insert a new vertex along with its associated edges and display the updated graph.

B. Deletion of an edge: Remove a selected edge from the graph and display the updated graph representation.

C. Degree and neighbours: Calculate and display the degree and direct neighbours of a selected vertex.

2. Objectives

1.To understand graph representation using an adjacency matrix.

2.To insert a new vertex and establish its connections with existing vertices.

3.To delete a selected edge and update the adjacency matrix.

4.To calculate the degree of a vertex and identify its direct neighbours.

5.To implement graph operations using the C programming language.

3. Algorithm

1.Start.
2.Read the number of vertices and the adjacency matrix.

3.Display the original adjacency matrix.

4.Insert a vertex:
Read the connections of the new vertex with existing vertices.
5.Update the corresponding row and column of the adjacency matrix.

6.Increase the number of vertices by one.

7.Display the updated graph.

8.Delete an edge:

Read the two vertices forming the selected edge.

9.Check whether the edge exists.

10.Set the corresponding matrix elements to zero.

11.Display the updated graph.

12.Find degree and neighbours:

Read the selected vertex.

13.Traverse its row in the adjacency matrix.

14.Count the entries equal to one to calculate the degree.

15.Display the vertices connected directly to it.

16.Stop.